      "claim": "The closest analogue, MP-10, is a CNS-penetrant PDE10A radioligand with specific, reversible striatal uptake in pig and baboon PET; the query shares the same 4-pyridyl-pyrazole-phenyl ether core, directly supporting meaningful brain access.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C10"],
      "claim": "In monkeys, MP-10 produced central pharmacodynamic effects after intravenous dosing, confirming that this chemotype reaches brain parenchyma at functionally relevant levels.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C09"],
      "claim": "A closely related quinolinylmethyl ether pyrazole analogue showed striatal brain uptake in rat biodistribution, providing additional transferable evidence for CNS access of this scaffold.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query is a close structural analogue of MP-10, a well-established brain-penetrant PDE10A ligand with PET-verified CNS uptake across species. Multiple related analogues also show brain penetration, and the shared pyridyl-pyrazole-phenyl ether pharmacophore supports meaningful CNS access despite moderate physicochemical liabilities.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct experimental measurement exists for the exact query molecule; the closest analogue differs by N-fluoroethyl versus N-methyl and methoxypyridine versus quinoline substituents.",
    "Quantitative brain-to-plasma ratios and P-gp efflux data are not available for the query itself."
  ],
